# Code owners for cookie-janitor.
#
# Every file in the repo has @sgireddy as owner by default. Since we
# are a single-maintainer project today, the value of this file is
# not who-reviews-what (there's only one reviewer) — it's:
#
#   * Setting up for future multi-maintainer growth: when a second
#     person joins, we add them here with a scoped pattern instead of
#     rewriting from scratch.
#
#   * Enabling the ruleset's optional `require_code_owner_review`
#     toggle later without a follow-up file scaffold.
#
#   * Documenting responsibility clearly for external contributors:
#     PRs get auto-requested from the owner instead of nobody.
#
# Syntax reference:
#   https://docs.github.com/en/repositories/managing-your-repositories-settings-and-features/customizing-your-repository/about-code-owners

# Default: everything belongs to the maintainer.
*                                @sgireddy

# Security-sensitive surfaces get called out explicitly so a future
# addition of a scoped reviewer (e.g. a security-focused contributor)
# is a one-line change here instead of a hunt through the tree.
/src/cookie_janitor/safety/      @sgireddy
/src/cookie_janitor/writers/     @sgireddy
/docs/THREAT_MODEL.md            @sgireddy
/SECURITY.md                     @sgireddy
/.github/                        @sgireddy
